### SMS API Tests
### Phase 5 - SMS Notification System

### Login to get token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test2@example.com",
  "password": "Test1234"
}

### Get SMS history
GET http://localhost:8080/api/sms/history
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Send test SMS (requires Twilio configuration)
# Note: Twilio credentials must be configured in admin_settings table
# - twilio_account_sid
# - twilio_auth_token
# - twilio_phone_number
POST http://localhost:8080/api/sms/test
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890"
}

### Send daily summary (requires Twilio configuration and user phone number)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/sms/send-daily-summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Instructions:
### 1. Login with the first request to get your JWT token
### 2. Replace {{token}} with the actual token value from the login response
### 3. Configure Twilio credentials in the database (see below)
### 4. Test SMS sending

### To configure Twilio (run these SQL commands via sqlite-web at http://localhost:8081):
# INSERT INTO admin_settings (key, value, category, isSecret) VALUES ('twilio_account_sid', 'YOUR_TWILIO_SID', 'sms', 1);
# INSERT INTO admin_settings (key, value, category, isSecret) VALUES ('twilio_auth_token', 'YOUR_TWILIO_TOKEN', 'sms', 1);
# INSERT INTO admin_settings (key, value, category, isSecret) VALUES ('twilio_phone_number', '+1234567890', 'sms', 0);
